WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.449 --> 00:00:06.489
At

2
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.119
its simplest form, network access control or N

3
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:10.430
A

4
00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:14.560
is a way to prevent unwanted devices from connecting to a network.

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.439
Some N

6
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.790
A systems allow for the installation of required software on

7
00:00:18.799 --> 00:00:22.549
the end user's device to enforce device compliance to policy.

8
00:00:22.559 --> 00:00:23.799
Prior to connecting

9
00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:25.879
a high level example of a NA

10
00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:28.510
AC system is hotel internet access.

11
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.270
Typically a user connecting to the hotel network is required to acknowledge

12
00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:37.229
the acceptable use policy before being allowed to access the internet.

13
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.810
After the user clicks the acknowledge button,

14
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.729
the device is connected to the network that enables internet access.

15
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.130
Some hotels add an additional layer requiring the guest to enter a special

16
00:00:48.139 --> 00:00:52.150
password or a room number and guest name before access is granted.

17
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.130
This prevents abuse by someone who is not a hotel guest and

18
00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:59.439
may even help to track network abuse to a particular user.

19
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.220
A slightly more complex scenario is a business that separates

20
00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:08.910
employee byod devices from corporate owned devices on the network.

21
00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:14.110
If the byod device is pre approved and allowed to connect to the corporate network,

22
00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:14.449
the

23
00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:19.349
NC system can validate the device using a hardware address or installed software

24
00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.190
and even check to make sure the antivirus software and operating system

25
00:01:23.199 --> 00:01:26.660
software are up to date before connecting it to the network.

26
00:01:27.089 --> 00:01:28.300
Alternatively,

27
00:01:28.309 --> 00:01:31.919
if it is a personal device not allowed to connect to the corporate network,

28
00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.370
it can be redirected to the guest network for

29
00:01:34.379 --> 00:01:38.230
internet access without access to internal corporate resources.